On Wednesday 12 October 2011 18:59:56 .alyn.post. wrote:
> This statement gives me an error in jbofihe:
>
>   $ echo "tu'o to toi"|jbofihe
>
> I assume that the above is valid Lojban, and that jbofihe is in
> error here: tu ... toi is in the free production, which should be
> able to appear nearly anywhere.
>
> Yes?

I tried a few other strings on jbofi'e. It appears that "to ... toi" cannot 
appear inside a string of letters or numbers. If you put "boi" after "tu'o", 
jbofi'e accepts it. I haven't checked it against the grammar.

